// Reading a field out of a LOCAL record whose type carries an arithmetic
// policy on ANY field has no Terminal plan. `Reading` omits at
// `structural field store: pure source: scalar expression row`; the same
// program with `b: i32` checks. Reduced from `samples/cli/simulation/grid_walk`.
//
// The phase label is the usual liar: construction is FINE. A local of this
// type that is never read plans; it is the READ that has no row. So does a
// read into another local, which omits at a different phase
// (`statement sequence: local data: scalar local: pure initializer`) —
// the destination is not what is missing, the SOURCE row is.
//
// What the bisect ruled out, each one alternated against its control:
//
//   arithmetic in the store (`self.qx = r.a + 1`)  irrelevant — a bare
//                                                  `r.a` omits identically
//   the value coming from a CALL                   irrelevant — a literal-
//                                                  built local omits too,
//                                                  and a call-bound SCALAR
//                                                  of policy type CHECKS
//   which field is read                            irrelevant — reading the
//                                                  PLAIN `a` omits just as
//                                                  reading the policy `b`
//   the DESTINATION's policy                       irrelevant — a plain
//                                                  destination behind a cast
//                                                  omits; a policy
//                                                  destination fed from an
//                                                  all-plain record checks
//   which policy                                   irrelevant — `Wrapping`
//                                                  omits like `Saturating`
//   `[copy]`                                       irrelevant — omits with
//                                                  and without
//   being a LOCAL                                  LOAD-BEARING — the same
//                                                  read off a self-held
//                                                  record field checks
//   a policy field EXISTING in the type            LOAD-BEARING — `b: i32`,
//                                                  `b: u8` and `b: bool` all
//                                                  check
//
// So the missing capability is one Terminal source row: a scalar field read
// whose carrier is an owned local of a record type that is not uniformly
// Exact. Whatever excludes it is keyed on the TYPE's policy content, not on
// the path being read, because the plain sibling field is refused with it.
use omega_language_std::console;
use omega::language::core::binding;

data Reading [copy] {
    a: i32;
    b: i32 in Saturating;
}

data Main {
    console: Binding<Console>;
    total: i32;
}

machine Main::accumulate(&mut self) {
    let reading: Reading = Reading { a: 1, b: 2 };
    self.total = reading.a;
}

machine Main::main(&mut self) reaches Console {
    self.total = 0;
    self.accumulate();
    self.console.exit_process(0);
}
